- op: discuss  # 4e9a
  at: '2026-09-16T07:10:20Z'  # 4e9a
  by: agent  # 4e9a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4e9a
  clock: 5  # 4e9a
  nonce: 4e9a  # 4e9a
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-09-16 by PR #994 (9d552f3bd1) + PR #995 (5467d2ed00). Behavioral\nevidence, this item's own filed repro re-run on dev 5467d2ed00.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO. This item's root_cause records \"removing 20 rows from go.yaml\nselected 2 test files, exited 0 in 4.4s, and missed 2 real failures in\ntest_io_boundary.py\". Editing io_primitives/go.yaml and running\nsmart-test --manifest now writes 158 selected tests, and test_io_boundary.py is\namong them.\n\nTHE 2026-09-15 PREDICTION ON THIS ITEM WAS EXACT and is what the fix was built\nagainst: \"a fix keyed on the io_primitives path alone would leave this one\nopen\". It did. function_summaries/go_stdlib.yaml -- the entry's own example,\nthe file whose dead-end markers decide whether a Go taint flow is REMOVED --\nselected 1 test then and selects 12 now. Every other family measured end to\nend: frameworks 0 -> 59, dataflow_patterns 0 -> 41, cfg_nodes 0 -> 79,\ntaint_sources 0 -> 143, taint_sanitizers 0 -> 143, library_signatures 0 -> 8,\nurl_folding 0 -> 7, io_primitives 157 -> 159.\n\nFIX SHAPE. Not (a) \"escalate to the full suite\" -- this item's later entry\nalready ruled that the wrong prescription once the cheaper mechanism existed --\nbut (c) generalised: derived from YAML_CATALOGS, the registry\nvalidate_registry() gates against the tree, so a new family is covered by the\ncommit that registers it rather than by an edit to the selector. The two\ndirectories this item named as \"consumed differently\" are handled by the\nregistry's own loader field: io_primitives resolves to io_boundary,\nfunction_summaries to function_summaries, and each family's tests are found by\ngrepping for its directory, its loader module, and that loader's load_* entry\npoints.\n\nTHE FOLD QUESTION RAISED HERE ON 2026-09-16 IS NOT RESOLVED BY THIS CLOSURE and\nis still the owner's. Both items are closed on their own filed rows with their\nown repros re-run, which is the \"close on the filed row\" rule rather than a\nruling on whether the two statements should have been one."  # 4e9a
